{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends","id":364994,"title":"What can we expect from Sothis Ascends?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-09T19:24:45-08:00","id":364994,"title":"What can we expect from Sothis Ascends?","content":"As I'm a bit of a late-comer to the <i>Mummy</i> party, I know tragically little about the future of the line. Sothis Ascends, Rio, Curse of the Blue Nile, and Dreams of Avarice are all that's left, right? Do we know anything about the content of these books? Will Sothis Ascends just be a collection of historical settings in the various Sothic Turns?<br /> <br /> I'd love to see some official wordcount go towards attempts by non-Iremite civilizations to harness sekhem and create Deathless/Lifeless of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T03:07:49-08:00","id":365253,"title":"","content":"All the specifics I remember are the Gentlemen Gamer writing a section for the Third Turn (about a kingdom that tried to eat Mummies or something), Dave B I think had to pass his writing over to Ian (I think), and...yeah, that's all I can recall at the moment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T03:18:45-08:00","id":365264,"title":"","content":"I three-quarters finished the First Turn, and passed it to Malcolm Sheppard, not Ian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T04:19:13-08:00","id":365294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends#post364994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm a bit of a late-comer to the <i>Mummy</i> party, I know tragically little about the future of the line. Sothis Ascends, Rio, Curse of the Blue Nile, and Dreams of Avarice are all that's left, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a novel too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T05:29:06-08:00","id":365326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=365264#post365264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I three-quarters finished the First Turn, and passed it to Malcolm Sheppard, not Ian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you. I think I get confused between them because of Jurassic Park and Jeff Goldblum's character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T07:52:55-08:00","id":365420,"title":"","content":"What can we expect from Sothis Ascends?<br /> <br /> Quality writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T17:40:17-08:00","id":365879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=365420#post365420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can we expect from Sothis Ascends?<br /> <br /> Quality writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree.<br /> <br /> For me, the existing Mummy writing has set a new high standard for WW/OPP products that I have trouble imagining any other book surpassing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T22:31:11-08:00","id":370763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends#post364994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm a bit of a late-comer to the <i>Mummy</i> party, I know tragically little about the future of the line. Sothis Ascends, Rio, Curse of the Blue Nile, and Dreams of Avarice are all that's left, right? Do we know anything about the content of these books? Will Sothis Ascends just be a collection of historical settings in the various Sothic Turns?<br /> <br /> I'd love to see some official wordcount go towards attempts by non-Iremite civilizations to harness sekhem and create Deathless/Lifeless of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Felipe mentioned there is a novel in the works too, but that's likely to be the last thing released. <br /> <br /> As for Sothis (since its the next book out I'll focus on the content of that one) its a setting book basically. It provides people the tools to run historical chronicles.<br /> <br /> Things I kinda-sorta remember about it:<br /> <br /> - It covers what important events happened to Arisen culture in the previous turns. <br /> - It details new relics, utterances and affinities<br /> - It provides stats for historical weapons/armour/tools<br /> - It's got a few new antagonist types beyond just Deceived, Shuankshen and Amkhata. <br /> <br /> Its been suggested that some of these new antagonists might be attempts by &quot;lesser&quot; cultures to repeat the Rite of Return and make themselves into Deathless beings. I expect most of them to be Lifeless entities. I kinda hope the Purified out of WoD: Immortals get a mention at least. <br /> <br /> The Utterances will have different powers for Arisen and Deceived were necessary. I believe the White Jackal from DC still has access to an Utterance that has yet to be published, so its likely to be in the book.<br /> <br /> Finally, there may be some more details on Apotheosis. That's a big maybe though, as such content might be more &quot;flavour text&quot; then anything and is more likely to be explored in Dreams of Avarice.<br /> <br /> As for the quality of writing for Mummy. Its good no doubt, but I'd hardly say its head and shoulder above the other recent books Onyx Path has released or is about to release. Demon's been consistently well written as well for example. Promethean SE looks like it going to have at least that level of polish as well. M20 is looking to blow everything that came before it out of the water quality wise. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T22:52:46-08:00","id":370770,"title":"","content":"I'll echo the thought that Mummy's writing quality is above everything else in recent memory; the lore in Book of the Deceived was flavorful enough to retroactively sell me on the rest of the line, and may well be my vote for best in the nWoD.<br /> <br /> Wordcount put towards non-Iremite immortals would be my favorite possible thing going forward (especially for Chinese and Mesoamerican mummies!), with mortal sorcerers as a close second. Sothis looks incredibly tasty, even if I doubt I'll ever run anything before Turn 3.<br /> <br /> Will Sothis (or any other book) cover Turn 0?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T01:27:02-08:00","id":370808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=370770#post370770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll echo the thought that Mummy's writing quality is above everything else in recent memory; the lore in Book of the Deceived was flavorful enough to retroactively sell me on the rest of the line, and may well be my vote for best in the nWoD.<br /> <br /> Wordcount put towards non-Iremite immortals would be my favorite possible thing going forward (especially for Chinese and Mesoamerican mummies!), with mortal sorcerers as a close second. Sothis looks incredibly tasty, even if I doubt I'll ever run anything before Turn 3.<br /> <br /> Will Sothis (or any other book) cover Turn 0?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To attempt to answer your questions (just going from my own supposition and the tid-bits I know about the line from scouring conversations here and on RPG.net since the games release):<br /> <br /> Sorcerers are either going to be detailed in Sothis or likely just left as a loose purely narrative idea within the scope of the Mummy line. Obviously one can adapt the systems from Second Sight or Witch Finders (for HtV) to represent them in that case. <br /> <br /> Non-Iremite immortals are likely to be covered, but as I mentioned they are framed as antagonists to the Arisen I believe and the majority of them are likely to be Lifeless (AKA bad mojo). Also, its been phrased that they are the result of bastardized rites that only knew distorted aspects of the true Rite of Return and aped the rest. So its very likely they are going to be a lot weaker then the Arisen in terms of template. I suspect they might match up with the &quot;base line&quot; Shaunkshen, maybe. Basically their cheap knock offs, or at least that's the impression I get, so don't expect them to be treated as the equals or peers of the &quot;true&quot; Deathless Arisen from Irem. <br /> <br /> I have a rough memory that apparently the Purified were originally going to get a quote in the Mummy core book in regards to the Arisen (it was mainly a reaction of horror) but it was cut for word count issues. Hence why I hope some of the existing Immortals in the WOD (Blood Bathers, Purified, Reapers etc) get at least a paragraph on how they view or might interact with the Arisen. <br /> <br /> To my knowledge Turn 0 is purposefully being left vague, as would require writing up a factual account of Irem for people to run. Considering that the truth about Irem and the motives of its rulers and guilds is always presented as incomplete and subjective, this is very unlikely to ever happen. Dreams of Avarice might have the closest thing to an &quot;objective&quot; point of view on the &quot;truth&quot; of Irem, the Shan'Iatu, the Guilds and the Rite. <br /> <br /> To clarify on the writing quality point:<br /> <br /> I'm not denying Deceived was well written, it was, thats just simple fact. Its still likely my 3rd favourite antagonist book after Pandora's Book (particularly the chapter on the Centimani) and Balials Brood. I simply feel it has several comparable books from other lines that are of equal quality. Then again, maybe I'm bias, as I have a rocky history with Mummy as an actualized game rather then as a collection of fiction and game ideas (in which I pretty much adore it). Perhaps most evident in that I seem to be the only person who's read Deceived and gone:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Yep that was good, didn't really do what I wanted with the Deceived, but its done something different and interesting with them that I can respect and do find evocative to the imagination.&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> Rather then:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Holy crap this is awesome and the best splat book ever for any line in any version of the WoD!&quot;</i> (OK I've fallen into hyperbole here, but you get the point I think) <br /> <br /> Mind you, it would not be a WoD gameline that did not have Vampire, Werewolf or Mage in the title if it did not have its die hard fans. I mean Promethean is niche as hell in the fan base of the wider WoD but I would walk through fire to defend some of the writing in the line. Likewise, the recent Wraith Kickstarter kinda crystallized the idea of a devoted &quot;cult&quot; fanbase that will stick with a game through the good and bad and will grow to be bigger then it might seem at first glance. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T04:09:01-08:00","id":370874,"title":"","content":"Personal preference in the writing is important too, from my perspective, and it's perfectly fine to recognize quality without thinking it's the best thing ever. <i>I </i>adored the Book Of The Deceived because the Mummy cosmology and the way it's written has really caught me ever since the core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=370808#post370808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerers are either going to be detailed in Sothis or likely just left as a loose purely narrative idea within the scope of the Mummy line. Obviously one can adapt the systems from Second Sight or Witch Finders (for HtV) to represent them in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be fine with them only being a narrative resource to use and represent as you please, but if they're ever going to be detailed they'll probably use Pillars as a power resource like Mummies, even if they don't have Sekhem. At least if the hints in the existing Mummy books (including one bit that mentions, and I quote &quot;soul-channelling sorcerers&quot; alongside the Arisen) are to be trusted.<br /> <br /> There's also very reliable ground to claim that technically the Mummies <i>were </i>once such mortal sorcerers, given the guilds were taught the (lesser) crafts of the Shan'iatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T04:22:19-08:00","id":370897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=370808#post370808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Holy crap this is awesome and the best splat book ever for any line in any version of the WoD!&quot;</i> (OK I've fallen into hyperbole here, but you get the point I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it's hyperbole if I've read half a dozen people actually have that opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:58:50-08:00","id":371153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=370897#post370897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if it's hyperbole if I've read half a dozen people actually have that opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't think anyone has laid on the praise quite as thick as my example, hence the hyperbole. <br /> <br /> Honestly, Deceived was the book out of the Mummy line I was looking forward to the most when the line details were announced. However, it was one of the most troubled development cycles of anything Onyx Path has ever put out. By the time it landed, I had my own idea of what the Deceived are and should be. so I was never going to go to be 100% happy unless some weird quirk of fate meant I had been sharing brain waves with the devs without knowing it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, its suffered (in my opinion, which I realize once again, is in a minority) from a certain inelegance in a lot of its mechanics. However, this is not so much an issue with that book as with the Mummy line as a whole since the core. Random dice pools with anywhere between 2-4 contributing stats or resistance pools for powers with no consistency does not make me a happy camper. Obviously there are my issues with how Memory is handled and the general fact that Mummy is still in WoD 1st Ed, but I've raised and discussed those points in other threads.<br /> <br /> The only pin-point issue i had was that the book actually did very little to expand the readers understanding of how the Deceived use name magic. It detailed the qualities that name magic has, and how the Deceived have powers that relate to those qualities (and use to have a lot more). It did not really make the Deceived any better at finding and using True Names. Nor did it make them any better then most at hiding from or protecting themselves from True Magic really (save one Utterance that did the latter...kinda)<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is massively off topic. So to steer things back on to topic:<br /> <br /> Basically, Sothis looks to be a very good tool kit for expanding the scope of any Mummy game. Likewise, I'm personally most looking forward to the addition of several other Antagonists to the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T14:03:26-08:00","id":371440,"title":"","content":"Just give me Chinese and Mesoamerican mummies, Lifeless or otherwise. I don't want to have to use Deceived or Twice Arisen for those all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T14:33:25-08:00","id":371457,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest the Blasphemous Depiction? It, or a similar relic, is the obvious method in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:14:30-08:00","id":371519,"title":"","content":"Regarding 'all attempts to create immortals past Irem resulted in Lifeless': doesn't that strike all y'all as some tasty propaganda? We know how much the Arisen and those they serve love the myth of Iremite exceptionalism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:26:34-08:00","id":371522,"title":"","content":"Book of the Deceived does make a pretty convincing argument in favour of Iremite exceptionalism, you have to admit.<br /> <br /> Unless there were Shan'iatu scattered all across the world as well...<br /> <br /> That could lead to a whole mess of Judges <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally, I love Mummy's strong focus as the product of a proto-Egyptian culture. Other ancient cultures as shadows of Irem are interesting, but I think the idea of Irem as the unique creation of a group of bitter demigods works better as an isolated incident. As has been said before, the idea that Mummy should share design space with corpses from other cultures just because the English word for all forms of preserved body is &quot;Mummy&quot; gets my hackles up a bit.<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping for mortal sorcerers in Sothis Ascends though. If they don't get any rules of their own, Seba can be repurposed easily enough to serve that purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:04:02-08:00","id":371559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=371519#post371519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding 'all attempts to create immortals past Irem resulted in Lifeless': doesn't that strike all y'all as some tasty propaganda?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it strikes me as heading off twee &quot;Four elements? But what about the Wu Xing?&quot; shenanigans. Insofar as it can be termed propaganda at all, it's of the sort that should prompt questions about how legitimate the difference is between Lifeless and Deathless, not &quot;did any other massive precursorial empires erase themselves from history in a fashion that just so happens to have produced mummies consistent with both the preserved human bodies discovered in those regions and their attendant mythology?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Rite of Return <i>broke time</i> to ensure the Arisen work as they do, and it was a massive bloody undertaking whose conclusion just so happens to coincide temporally with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5.9_kiloyear_event\" target=\"_blank\"><i>the beginning of the latest desertification of the Sahara</i>.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-15-2015, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T19:33:25-08:00","id":371711,"title":"","content":"Mechanics is one of the areas I appreciate what Mummy brings. While the different stat rolls did stand out to me I tend to look at that in games as oddity vs bad mechanics. It's one of things I'd like to pick writers brains about because often times the answer is either someone picked it(or development asked for it) or there is a specific reason why those stats are used. What I have enjoyed about the mechanics is that so many of the powers work well with the mood the game is seeking to create. I don't know how many of the powers he has written but it's an area Michael Goodwin has hit very very well in the material for White Wolf/Onyx Path I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T19:45:49-08:00","id":371721,"title":"","content":"Aye, I concur in that Mummy's odd power mechanics definitely come off as a feature, not a bug. You don't have to be playing long to recognise the patterns. Powers that include Sekhem are often extremely strong... for a little while. Those that include several additional stats to roll in addition to Sekhem (Secrets Ripped from Skies Tier 2, for example), are clearly designed to peak at high Sekhem and decline, but remain strong even at low Sekhem. Powers without Sekhem included in their pool (Tier 1 Words of Dead Glory, for example) are evidently designed to be equally strong irrespective of the user's current Sekhem trait. Powers that are just Sekhem, or Sekhem+one other trait, are meant to be heavily influenced in strength by the Descent and become dramatically weaker within a few scenes of the first session (see Power of Re Tier 3).<br /> <br /> There's a very clear intent behind the lack of uniformity in Mummy's powers, and I am more than happy to forfeit a sense of cohesiveness for the excellent ways in which these mechanics integrate with the game on a thematic level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T00:37:27-08:00","id":372080,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> <br /> As I said, I personally find the mechanics clunky, unintuitive and messy, but that's just me. I like uniformity and consistency in my systems and I find coherency and simplicity aesthetically pleasing. However, as I said before, that's just my personal taste, so its not something I expect everyone to agree on. <br /> <br /> Though I have said it before in other threads I'll repeat it here: I've been living and breathing God-Machine, Strix and Demon for the last 9-12 months. Not to mention following the open dev for Werewolf, Mage and Promethean. So I am just much more involved with the 2nd Ed system now. <br /> <br /> While mechanically its very similar obviously, I feel that the 2nd Ed games are much more streamlined in their content then the 1st Ed versions were. Looking at the very storyteller friendly system for Embeds in Demon for example were every power is two stat (attribute + skill) and most of them that invoke a resistance roll (which is left in the hands of the ST, not as a hard rule) are penalized rather then resisted. Very simple to learn and very friendly to not bogging down play looking up unique rolls for each power. <br /> <br /> Basically, I'm following Mummy because I feel the core idea about identity and Memory is awesome. The writing is good, the setting, worldbuilding and general &quot;fluff&quot; text is great. Do I think I'm ever going to run it as an actual game ever again while its in its 1st Ed iteration? Hell no. I'm happy to bask in the setting until the 2nd Ed comes out in 2-3 years and streamlines the whole thing nicely (hopefully). <br /> <br /> Not to mention hopefully give us a more inclusive Core book. Since Mummy got short changed in page count. The Vampire 2nd Ed (which Werewolf is supposedly about the same size as) is about 320 pages. Thats a full 50 more then Mummy. So hopefully the extra space in Mummy 2nd Ed will let us get the rules for Vestiges (from DC), Relic Architecture and the Deceived (obviously in a cut down form, though second ed might simply their system as well) in the core. If not just a little more space for Relics in general (and the Shuankshen maybe) and actual example Nomes for various cities of interest to the Arisen around the world. <br /> <br /> Anyway, so this post was not completely off topic:<br /> <br /> The rules for Relic Architecture are supposed to be in Sothis I believe. Just remembered that.<br /> <br /> DC has a few examples of Relic Architecture, but it mentions the full rules for creating Relic Architecture will be in a later Mummy book. I presume this is Sothis. Will be nice to have the rules, as it will let people playing Tef-Aahbi finally do some more active Geomancy stuff that's not just flavour text. <br /> <br /> Also on Sorcerers:<br /> <br /> I feel we have a lot of ways of modeling these guys without even stepping out of the Mummy line. Giving them a Pillars pool and some Utterance abilities is just the most obvious. Affinities, Seba and Pillar powers for the Fasid/Sadikh could all represent this stuff as well. <br /> <br /> As I said before if you include a couple of non-Mummy books: Second Sight (core WoD 1st Ed), Immortals (core WoD 1st Ed), Reliquary (core WoD 1st Ed) and Witch Hunters (HtV) you get a lot more options too. When I ran Mummy I used a fan-hack for a Second Sight Tradition and some elements of the &quot;Eternal&quot; type of &quot;lesser&quot; Immortal from Immortals. If I ran it again I'd likely use Witch Hunters system for Gutter Magic. <br /> <br /> Oh, something I do hope is included in Sothis Ascends:<br /> <br /> Bane Relics<br /> <br /> We've had one so far in Guildhalls and it was awesome. I kinda like the idea of Ammut being a bit more active in supporting the Shaunkshen and these fit the bill awesomely. That being said, I'd also like some more Bane Affinities too. A pipe dream would be some Bane Utterances, but that's not likely to happen I suspect. <br /> <br /> Basically more &quot;Bane&quot; stuff in Sothis and Rio will make me pretty happy really. We know from Deceived that Ammut can't really interact with the world directly anymore, but having her as a terrible eldrich presence and patron of the Shaunkshen works nicely in the setting I feel. <br /> <br /> In a similar line of thought, example Duat entities of a lesser magnitude then the Judges, Ammut and Shezmu would also be kinda nice to have. As I kinda like the idea of Sorcerers conjuring up Slaughterers and other lesser demons. <br /> <br /> Sothis seems like the only place these things could go now really. As they don't really fit in a setting book like Rio or a prop book like Avarice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T02:30:01-08:00","id":372140,"title":"","content":"So from Sothis I expect new Affinities , Relics and Utterances.<br /> Historical settings, how the Arisen infiltrares other cultures, examples of Iremite influence.<br /> New antagonists, new Lifeless and mortal sorcerers rules.<br /> More information on Apotheosis and the Ladder of Seth.<br /> Awesomeness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T02:35:12-08:00","id":372143,"title":"","content":"Anyway its in Editing and already art directed as of the latest Monday Meeting. Shall we expect it by the end of February?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T03:48:23-08:00","id":372188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>atamajakki:</b> Just give me Chinese and Mesoamerican mummies, Lifeless or otherwise. I don't want to have to use Deceived or Twice Arisen for those all the time. </div> </div> </div>I think, given what the Arisen have turned out to be, that the mummies of other cultures would be better represented as a whole different creature - even if you borrowed some mechanics for it - at least as different as the Kuei-jin were from Masquerade's Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T05:06:28-08:00","id":372212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=372140#post372140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from Sothis I expect new Affinities , Relics and Utterances.<br /> Historical settings, how the Arisen infiltrares other cultures, examples of Iremite influence.<br /> New antagonists, new Lifeless and mortal sorcerers rules.<br /> More information on Apotheosis and the Ladder of Seth.<br /> Awesomeness</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say definitely Affinities, Relics and Utterances (with Deceived versions of some)<br /> I'd say definitely to historical settings (kinda the point of the book) and the Arisen's activities in those times<br /> I'd say definitely new antagonists some of whom are likely to be Lifeless.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer rules are a big maybe at the moment I think.<br /> <br /> Apotheosis and the Ladder of Seth are more likely to be covered in Dreams of Avarice, since that is the journal/bible of the Heretic, the only Mummy to achieve Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Looking back on this thread, its interesting that Gentleman Gamer has written about a Cult of people that tried to steal a Mummy's power by eating them. Very similar to the Faithful of Shulpae from the Hunter book Mortal Remains. Likewise, sounds like a cult with a possible link the Shaunkshen.<br /> <br /> I'd say March is a safer bet for Sothis, M20 is taking up loads of Mike Chaney's time at the moment. Combine that with V20 DA proofs, Werewolf 2nd Ed and the Dark Era's Kickstarter work and the guys run off his feet. Not to mention it still needs to get out of editing.<br /> <br /> Personally, since its obvious that the Mummy devs like to focus on one project at a time, I'll be interested to see how quickly Rio gets through the various stages of development once Sothis is out. I'm kinda hoping Sothis, Rio, Dreams and Curse of the Blue Nile can all be in our hands (or on our computers) by October.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 01-16-2015, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T05:18:23-08:00","id":372214,"title":"","content":"The Faithful of Shulpae were the cannibal Hunters. I think it's doubling interesting, because around the time Mortal Remains came out there was a developer saying that they clearly weren't eating Arisen Mummies because the flesh of Mummies couldn't be consumed (a bit of a weird argument, really, in a setting where a set of antagonists already exists with that precise ability).<br /> <br /> Anyway, I have players that are positively salivating at the prospect of new powers in Sothis, so that's most of what I'm looking forward to. Relics, even Bane Relics, I could take or leave. Most exist for inspiration more than any actual use in my games. A new antagonist could be cool, but I have by-and-large written my game setting and any new villains would simply be diversions and minor encounters at this point. So... yeah, the previous Turns are of interest for flashback potential, but other than that I'm mostly looking forward to new Affinities and Utterances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T05:40:10-08:00","id":372221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/364994-what-can-we-expect-from-sothis-ascends?p=372080#post372080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a similar line of thought, example Duat entities of a lesser magnitude then the Judges, Ammut and Shezmu would also be kinda nice to have. As I kinda like the idea of Sorcerers conjuring up Slaughterers and other lesser demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. A smorgasbord of affinities, utterances, and relics I think was part of the blurb we got upon announcement. But my big hopes are 1) <b>Mummy</b>-specific rules for mortal sorcerers and 2) Lifeless antagonists - even just two would make me drool: some type of demon from Duat/Anpu's dominion, and some other bastard-type of Mummy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:15:19-08:00","id":372785,"title":"","content"